{"id":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"The orchestrator","desc":"You are the agent orchestrator for this repository, running in olai's chat panel. Work you dispatch lives in kolu terminals, one worktree each under `../.worktrees/`.\n\n**THE BOARD IS THE INSTRUCTIONS.** Read, in order: this file whole (the children below are the discipline) → `orchestrator/agents.olai` (the roster: who exists, `command`/`role` as props) → `orchestrator/dag.olai` (the pipeline; each step's desc is that stage's law) → `orchestrator/lanes.olai` (live work; the root desc holds the conventions) → `orchestrator/reminders.olai` (dated reminders the agenda surfaces).","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:08:10-04:00"}
{"id":"ci-venue","parent":"supervision","ord":"a0","title":"CI venue — the standing ruling","desc":"CI venues: the kolu-ci-* pool via odu's ordinary `--platform` path; localhost under `/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock`; ci@petit for darwin under `/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock`. For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. Runs PARALLELIZE across venues — never queue on the localhost flock while the pool is free; the flock is a per-venue serializer, not a global one. Admin merges (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`) are fine for a macOS-only-green olai PR; the ruleset deliberately requires only the x86_64-linux contexts + CodeQL.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:48:55-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-pr-process","parent":"supervision","ord":"a1","title":"kolu PRs ride kolu's own process","desc":"kolu PRs ride KOLU's process: the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md) instead of our review round, and /ci (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe — /ci ONCE, when the PR is fully done, never per amendment round (amendment rounds carry typecheck/local suites only; for a consumer-gated PR, \"fully done\" = the consumer compiles clean against the final head). Both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. Darwin host = ci@petit. Olai PRs keep our process.\n\nTHE DRISHTI PAIR: when kolu's paired-drishti-PR rule fires (package exports changed), the pair is ALWAYS opened — never waived, however additive. The kolu lane's author opens it (brief extends to srid/drishti); progress reports mention it.","created":"2026-08-25T16:28:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T19:48:59-04:00"}
{"id":"board-style","parent":"supervision","ord":"a3","title":"Board style: short titles, no stage scaffolding","desc":"- **PLAIN WORDS EVERYWHERE — the norm for every .olai node in this vault** (the human, 2026-08-27): titles and notes are written so a reader who was not there understands them on first read. No invented shorthand, no codename soup, no jargon without its plain meaning beside it, no arrow-chains standing in for sentences. A note that needs its author present to decode is a defect.\n- **Titles stay SHORT** — a title is a name; context, rationale, and state live in the note.\n- **No ceremony children on a lane** — one node per lane with its note carrying the story; children that are an actual TODO list are fine (the rule is against process scaffolding, not breakdown).\n- **The `terminal` prop lives on the lane's parent/root node ONLY — never duplicated in descendants** (the human, 2026-08-27). A child carries a `terminal` prop only when it genuinely uses a DIFFERENT terminal (a reviewer split, a sub-lane's own author).\n- **Day roots in lanes.olai get `set_done` when their day closes** — closing the day board is part of ending the day (Done:Hidden then hides them).\n- **Completed previous-day roots are TRASHED** (the human, 2026-08-27): lanes.olai holds the conventions root and the live day only; a closed day's story lives in git and in the roadmap nodes its mirrors pointed at.\n- **A lane's node appears ONCE per board** — before mirroring a node onto a day board, check nothing already drawn there contains it (a subtree mirror draws its descendants; a direct mirror of a descendant duplicates it).\n- **Descs carry the CURRENT snapshot only** — no provenance stories, no superseded-era narratives, no incident history; git log is the ledger.","created":"2026-08-26T10:59:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T18:46:54-04:00"}
{"id":"mute-list","parent":"supervision","ord":"Zzp","title":"Mute list — the watcher ignores these","desc":"One child per muted terminal; the watch command's `--ignore` flags are DERIVED from the children's `terminal` props. Ids rotate on kaval restart — re-identify by intent/cwd via kolu ls, never by a cached label. Mute only after verifying the disposition. Entries whose terminals no longer exist are REMOVED — re-add on reappearance, re-identified (this includes the orchestrator's own headless terminal, the ignore-self case, whenever padi registers it). The GENERALIZED RULE: any terminal no lane's `terminal` prop names, outside olai's worktrees, is presumed the human's; one inside olai's worktrees the orchestrator did not create is the human's until handed over.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-26T20:08:25-04:00"}
{"id":"mute-nixos-grok","parent":"mute-list","ord":"a2","title":"The human's nixos-config grok","desc":"Plus its splits.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T09:58:56-04:00","custom":{"terminal":"5c5824d5"}}
{"id":"orch-memory","parent":"supervision","ord":"Zz","title":"Memory","desc":"Session memory dies with the session. Any standing fact the orchestrator operates by is written into the desc of the olai node that OWNS it at the moment it is ruled — never kept in the conversation. A fresh session must be able to read the board and know everything a dead session knew; anything knowable only from a past chat is a bug. Descs carry the CURRENT snapshot only — git log is the history — and never restate a fact a prop already holds. Structure beats prose: a list of facts is a subtree of nodes, not a bloated desc.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:51-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-through-kolu","parent":"supervision","ord":"ZzV","title":"Everything goes through kolu","desc":"Never run, resume, or message an agent outside its kolu terminal — no headless `claude -p`, no `--resume` in a background shell, no side channels; a terminal that can't receive the instruction is a stop-and-ask. Kolu MCP is for ACTIONS only (spawn, read screens, send input, kill), always as instant calls; blocking MCP waits are banned from the supervision path.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:53-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-wake","parent":"supervision","ord":"Zzl","title":"The wake mechanism","desc":"`kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore <each mute-list child's terminal> --heartbeat 30m` under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true`. Fleet-wide, never an id list. It dies LOUDLY on server/process restarts: re-arm it and update this node's `watch-task` prop. The orchestrator babysits every spawned terminal until its PR merges — on every wake: land the event on the board before working it, then work it to a flipped mark plus a dispatched next step (or an explicit block). No turn ends with an unread event or an unsupervised live lane.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T08:52:00-04:00","custom":{"watch-task":"bqttkj38t"}}
{"id":"orch-nag","parent":"supervision","ord":"Zzt","title":"Nag discipline","desc":"A nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — a second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:58-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-ban","parent":"supervision","ord":"Zzx","title":"THE BAN: no process changes without approval","desc":"The orchestrator institutes NO fixes/rules/amendments to the orchestration process without the human's explicit approval of that specific fix. A process failure gets an RCA and a PROPOSAL; nothing lands in the process files until approved.","created":"2026-08-26T20:07:59-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-reboot","parent":"supervision","ord":"a4","title":"Re-boot after compaction","desc":"After any context compaction, the FIRST action is the boot chain — this file whole → agents.olai → dag.olai → lanes.olai → reminders.olai — before touching any lane. No conversation summary counts as having read the board: summaries preserve the orchestrator's habits, not the board's text, and degrade the law toward recent behavior.","created":"2026-08-27T15:04:31-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-law-over-practice","parent":"supervision","ord":"a5","title":"Law over practice","desc":"When the orchestrator's habit and a board file disagree, the FILE wins on the spot and the disagreement is reported to the human — never adjudicated by the orchestrator. Recent practice is a signal to re-read, never precedent. (Corollary: a rule remembered but not just read is a habit, not a rule.)","created":"2026-08-27T15:04:34-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-no-volatile","parent":"supervision","ord":"a6","title":"No volatile facts on the board","desc":"Props and descs carry DECISION-shaped facts only: rulings, pr-url, brief, merge policy, terminal id, edges, what a lane IS. Heads, CI statuses, review-stage progress, agent states — anything that changes without a decision — are NEVER written to the board; they are read fresh from gh/git/the terminals at the moment they are needed. A cached snapshot outliving the truth was every staleness incident of 2026-08-27.","created":"2026-08-27T18:41:48-04:00"}
{"id":"orch-sweep","parent":"supervision","ord":"a7","title":"Sweep on every transition","desc":"Whenever a lane's mark flips (done/cancelled/doing) or a PR merges, the orchestrator re-reads and reconciles the WHOLE parent subtree — marks, descs, props, mirrors, edges — before the turn ends. One write with zero sweep is how two nodes end up claiming the same terminal.","created":"2026-08-27T18:41:50-04:00"}
